&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Druva&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Druva is the resilience foundation for the AI enterprise, helping organizations secure and recover from connected risk across data, cyber, identity, and AI. The Resilience Cloud is a fully managed, cloud-native SaaS platform that delivers air-gapped and immutable protection across cloud, SaaS, on-premises, endpoint, and edge environments. Powered by Dru MetaGraph, Druva’s graph-powered intelligence layer, the platform connects critical business context so customers can understand risk, respond faster, recover cleanly, and govern data with greater confidence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Trusted by nearly 7,500 customers, including 75 of the Fortune 500, Druva helps safeguard the critical information and systems businesses depend on in an increasingly connected world.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.druva.com/&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;druva.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and follow us on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/druva/mycompany/&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/druvainc&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/DruvaInc/&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This position is on a hybrid schedule, minimum Tues./Wed./Thurs. at Druva&#39;s Santa Clara HQ office.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Purpose &amp;amp; Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Manager, Corporate FP&amp;amp;A owns Druva&#39;s consolidated financial picture: the total company P&amp;amp;L, cash flow, balance sheet forecast and long-range plan. You&#39;ll report to the VP of Finance and lead a small, high-impact team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on leadership role at the center of the finance organization. You&#39;ll pull inputs from GTM, R&amp;amp;D, G&amp;amp;A and cost of revenue planning into one integrated view of the business. You&#39;ll own the company-level forecast and the Annual Operating Plan (AOP) consolidation, and build the financial narrative for the CFO, the executive team and the board.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be joining at a moment of real opportunity: we&#39;re refreshing our planning processes, raising the bar on forecast accuracy, and using AI to make FP&amp;amp;A faster and more insightful.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Corporate FP&amp;amp;A team at Druva serves as the strategic engine for the company&#39;s financial growth. The team is highly visible and deeply collaborative, partnering directly with executive leadership, the board, and global business units to translate complex data into actionable strategies. Driven by a low-ego, high-ownership mindset, the team&#39;s culture balances rigorous, data-backed financial discipline with rapid execution to support Druva&#39;s scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wh

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Elastic, the Search AI Company, enables everyone to find the answers they need in real time, using all their data, at scale — unleashing the potential of businesses and people. The Elastic Search AI Platform, used by more than 50% of the Fortune 500, brings together the precision of search and the intelligence of AI to enable everyone to accelerate the results that matter. By taking advantage of all structured and unstructured data — securing and protecting private information more effectively — Elastic’s complete, cloud-based solutions for search, security, and observability help organizations deliver on the promise of AI.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What is The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are on the lookout for a Senior Kubernetes/Go Engineer to join our Elasticsearch team and focus on ensuring that the shared platform functionalities of Elasticsearch are easy to use, performant, maintainable and secure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team’s mission is to create foundational infrastructure and shared functionality that enables engineers to develop, extend, and support Elasticsearch. The team owns common functionality such as services, settings and scripting, and makes Elasticsearch extensible through plugins or the Painless scripting language. The team also makes Elasticsearch observable by providing logging and telemetry information. We also own the orchestration of Elasticsearch in serverless, the CI/CD workflows and enable Elasticsearch developers to deliver Elasticsearch to customers - serverless, cloud and on-premise alike.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be a strong individual contributor on the team but you will also contribute to and lead cross team projects. We need someone who has great design skills, who can work at a low level of abstraction but can equally drive and communicate technical concepts across a variety of collaborators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing, building, and evolving the distributed systems that orchestrate and manage Serverless Elasticsearch projects across cloud service providers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to large, impactful projects that evolve the core infrastructure that underpins Elasticsearch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the Kubernetes orchestration of Elasticsearch clusters in cloud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Making Elasticsearch developers more productive by identifying and developing opportunities for automation, and integrating agentic apps into development workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing and implementing new horizontally-scalable features and APIs in Elasticsearch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solving difficult issues, including performance or concurrency issues, and proposing solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving operation and observability of Elasticsearch cloud systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating in the open with the ES

